---
import Icon from "@components/Icon.astro";
---

<section id="how-it-works" class="how-esphome-works">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="columns">
      <div class="content content-container">
        <h2>How ESPHome works!</h2>
        <p>
          Building your own smart home device from scratch can feel daunting, particularly if you’re not familiar with
          coding. Not with ESPHome. Its intuitive <a
            href="https://esphome.io/blog/2026/07/02/unbox-your-creativity-with-the-esphome-device-builder/"
            >Device Builder</a
          > replaces code with simple visual choices, guided by our desktop app for a hassle-free setup that brings you straight
          into the builder without touching a command line. And for experienced users who prefer writing code manually, YAML
          is always there if you need it.
        </p>

        <p>Whether you’re building your first sensor or managing fifty devices, the initial workflow stays the same…</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__title--icon-row">
            <Icon icon="manufacturing" class="card__icon" inline />
            <p class="card__title card__title--has-icon">Step 1: Choose & configure</p>
          </div>
          <p>
            Select your board and components using the visual Device Builder or a YAML file. Pick sensors from the
            catalog and set your options without writing code.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__title--icon-row">
            <Icon icon="build" class="card__icon" inline />
            <p class="card__title card__title--has-icon">Step 2: Build & install</p>
          </div>
          <p>
            ESPHome installs your configuration to your device straight from your browser, or wirelessly over the air.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__title--icon-row">
            <Icon icon="automation" class="card__icon" inline />
            <p class="card__title card__title--has-icon">Step 3: Connect & control</p>
          </div>
          <p>
            Your new device automatically pops up in Home Assistant over your local network: no cloud accounts or
            external servers required.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
  @use "../../styles/mixins" as *;

  .how-esphome-works {
    .columns {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 48px;
      margin: 0 auto;

      @include bp(tablet) {
        flex-direction: row;
      }
    }

    .content,
    .cards {
      @include bp(tablet) {
        flex-basis: 50%;
      }

      @include bp(desktop) {
        flex-basis: 55%;
      }
    }

    .cards {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.75rem;

      @include bp(desktop) {
        flex-basis: 45%;
      }
    }

    .card {
      padding: 1.25rem 1.75rem;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;

      &__title--icon-row {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
      }
    }
  }
</style>
